{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-6cd5a19a3da4", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:38:50.480Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 0, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:38:58.029Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 13375, "tokens_out": 102, "latency": 7.525, "finish_reason": "tool_use"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "What is the fraud referral procedure, and at what point does a claim have to be referred?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:c41eae1b6df85dd983a6d0ffba0a08a6dfe3f2fbe0e42bfdec85cc5c09acf816", "response_text": "I'll search for information about Thornfield Mutual's fraud referral procedure.", "response_hash": "sha256:d79af58de77baaca7b12de1998b1c0bbb85bd3da8278a866d21ccf22ceeca889", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-6cd5a19a3da4", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:38:50.480Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 1, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:38:58.294Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 14611, "tokens_out": 336, "latency": 0.2648, "finish_reason": "end_turn"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "What is the fraud referral procedure, and at what point does a claim have to be referred?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:c41eae1b6df85dd983a6d0ffba0a08a6dfe3f2fbe0e42bfdec85cc5c09acf816", "response_text": "Based on Thornfield Mutual's fraud referral procedure (prc-fraud-002):\n\n## When to refer\n\nReferral is warranted where **two or more** of the following indicators are present, or where **any one of them is strongly present**:\n\n- The policy was taken out or increased within thirty days of the incident\n- The incident happened at an unusual hour with no independent witness\n- Documents supplied are copies where originals would be expected, or carry inconsistent dates, fonts or reference numbers\n- The claimant is unusually familiar with policy wording or claims process\n- The same address, bank account or telephone number appears on unconnected claims\n- Injuries reported do not match the damage to the vehicle or property\n- The claimant presses for a quick cash settlement and declines an inspection\n- Receipts are sequential, from a single supplier, and round numbered\n\n## The procedure\n\nWhen you spot these indicators:\n- **Raise a referral** on the counter fraud queue\n- **Carry on handling** the claim normally\n- **Do not tell the claimant** a referral has been made\n- **Do not mention** the referral or reasons for it in any correspondence to the claimant\n\nThe counter fraud team will acknowledge within two working days and give one of three outcomes: no further action, monitor, or investigate. If they decide to investigate, all contact with the claimant passes to them and you stop corresponding. Payments cannot be made on a claim under investigation without written agreement from the counter fraud lead.", "response_hash": "sha256:d8606d739511ecbe4d6d38e2ac5ac80827b8566c4805cbb4bad170559de46541", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
